{
  "slug": "youth-employment",
  "title": "Youth Employment - Cross Party Group",
  "purpose": "The Cross-Party Group on Youth Employment exists to provide a forum for Members of the Senedd and external stakeholders to work collaboratively to promote improved employment outcomes for young people across Wales. The CPG will seek to champion youth employment as a national priority throughout the Seventh Senedd, recognising the significant social and economic benefits of enabling all young people to access good-quality employment, training and progression opportunities. The CPG aims to: • Champion youth employment as a national priority. • Address barriers facing young people, particularly those who are most disadvantaged. • Support the development of a future-ready workforce. • Promote collaboration between policymakers, employers, education providers, employers and the third sector. • Ensure the lived experiences of young people help inform policy and decision-making. The CPG will facilitate discussion, share evidence and best practice, and identify opportunities to improve opportunities and outcomes for young people throughout the Seventh Senedd.",
